    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōclīnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		proclino, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a bending</i> or <i>inclining
			forwards</i>: in concreto, <i>a slope</i>, <i>declivity</i> (Vitruvian), <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
				12, 4</span></i>.— In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne structurae habeant ullā in parte
					proclinationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					6, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
